(d)
Reimbursable Expenses. Any sum which is designated specifically in this
Lease as a “Reimbursable Expense” for which the Landlord is to be paid by Tenant shall, ifowed,
be paid by Tenant to Landlord each year on or before December 31.
5.
Security.
(a)
Security Deposit. Intentionally omitted.
(b)
Lien and Security Interest. Intentionally omitted.
6.
Use.
(a)
General. The Premises shall be used and occupied only for the Permitted
Uses set forth in Paragraph 1 above and for no other purpose, except as expressly consented to by
the Landlord in writing, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld.
(b)
Compliance with Law.
Effective as of the Commencement Date and
thereafter throughout the Term of this Lease, Tenant shall, at Tenant’s sole cost and expense,
comply with all relevant and applicable present and future laws, ordinances, orders, declarations
of covenants and restrictions, rules, regulations and requirements of all federal, state, county and
municipal governments, courts, departments, commissions, boards and officers, which may be
applicable to the Tenant’s business uses and activities on the Premises, and the sidewalk and curbs
adjoining the Premises or to the use or manner of use of the Premises (“Applicable Laws”).
Tenant shall not use or permit the use of the Premises in any manner that will tend to create waste
or a nuisance. Tenant agrees to obtain any and all necessary permits and licenses for Tenant’s
business and activities on the Premises prior to execution of this Lease or within a reasonable time
thereafter.
(c)
Existing Title and Condition of Premises.
Tenant hereby accepts the
Premises “AS IS” and “WHERE IS” physical condition, with the rights to make changes to the
Premises set out in this Lease and subject to all Applicable Laws. Tenant represents that Tenant
has, prior to execution of this Lease, inspected the Premises and found it suitable for Tenant’s
purposes.
Tenant agrees that neither Landlord nor Landlord’s agents have made
any
representations or warranties as to the Premises, including without limitation, any representation
or warranty as to the condition or fitness of the Improvements or the suitability of the
Improvements for the conduct of Tenant’s business.
(d)
Signs. Tenant may erect or install on any exterior or interior window, any
door, or any exterior wall any signs, advertising media, placards, trademarks, drapes, screens,
tinting materials, shades, blinds or similar items, without first securing the Landlord’s prior
permission. All signs shall comply with all Applicable Laws. Tenant shall properly maintain all
signs. Upon expiration of the Lease, Tenant shall remove all signs placed in and around the
Premises by Tenant and shall repair any damage to the Premises caused by the removal of such
signs within a reasonable time.
Lease Agreement
