```text
7.
Maintenance and Repairs.
(a)
Tenant’s Maintenance. Tenant shall not be responsible to maintain or pay
for maintenance allocated in subparagraph 7(b) below to the Landlord. Tenant shall at Tenant’s
sole cost and expense, keep and maintain the Premises in good order and repair and in a safe and
clean condition, including, without limitation: the exterior and interior portions of all doors,
windows, plate glass, store frontage, plumbing and sewage facilities (including drains) within the
Premises, fixtures, electrical systems, sprinkler system, walls paint or wall coverings, floor
coverings, ceiling paint or coverings, meters applicable to and located on the Premises, electrical,
plumbing and HVAC and/or boiler systems, any and all alterations and additions made to the
Premises by the Tenant pursuant to this Lease, all walks, driveways, parking and loading areas,
lawns and landscaping (if any), fences and signs located on or included with the Premises. While
this Lease is in effect, the Tenant shall further maintain and bear the expense of the light fixtures
and bulbs, janitorial services, interior pest control, and the like. Tenant shall not cause or permit
accumulation of any debris or extraneous matter on the roof of the Premises. In accordance with
any applicable municipal regulations, and its own expense, Tenant shall place any rubbish or other
matter outside the building on the Premises only in such containers as are authorized from time to
time by Landlord; see that there are no undue accumulations of garbage and refuse; and keep the
Premises (including, all exterior surfaces and both sides of all glass) clean, orderly, sanitary, and
free from objectionable odors, insects, vermin and other pests. Tenant shall, at Tenant’s own
expense, immediately replace all interior, exterior or other glass in or about the Premises that may
be broken during the Term with glass at least equal to the specification and quality of the glass so
replaced. If Tenant fails to perform Tenant’s obligations under this subparagraph, Landlord may
at its option enter upon the Premises after ten (10) days prior written notice to Tenant and put the
